From 65cb3d031341f89a05769244837975404d11e835 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:27:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/21] Make Fusion runtime records actionable for export and
 debugging

Carry object identity through durable records, tighten prepared-directory validation, and expose bounded walk/force diagnostics. Add DexCache namespace discovery so current Fusion can recover classes that are absent from loaded tables without reintroducing old global state.

Constraint: Preserve the existing no-execute capture contract and helper-owned output boundary.
Rejected: Porting the legacy monolithic dump path | It bypasses current staging and security boundaries.
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
Directive: Keep future discovery sources bounded and route them through the shared capture pipeline.
Tested: r0dump_f7_class_loader_walk_source_test.py; r0dump_config_boundary_source_test.py; git diff --check.
Not-tested: Full ART/AOSP build; lunch release configuration is unavailable in this checkout.
Change-Id: I1ce439bc30f8bd93245c037dbec8f151ca2d3461
